# `hi --packages-preview` renders what the priorities below do: each one's
# colors, a real example of each from this file, then the check itself.
# _HI_PACKAGES_MIN_PRIORITY is the dial that decides how far down the list you
# want to hear about. It ships at 2, so tiers 0-1 are hidden; above 3 mutes all.

#[-|+]group,package:priority,package2:priority2...
# a leading `-` speaks only when the whole line is missing, `+` only when one
# of it is installed; no flag speaks both ways. Priorities run 0-3, loudest
# last; on a line nothing satisfies, the max priority listed is the one used.

